{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If the length of data is not a multiple of size, the final partial chunk is yielded.\n    If size is larger than the length of data, a single chunk containing all data is yielded.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Yields:\n        bytes: Chunks of data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Chunk size must be positive\")\n    if not data:\n        return\n    # If size is larger than data length, yield data once\n    if size >= len(data):\n        yield data\n        return\n    for i in range(0, len(data), size):\n        yield data[i:i + size]\n","expected_sha256":"63673bc4c4b5f3784f5270c01c351b1e00cafd26bf90fdc78a333aebf432ab23","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Added explicit check for size <= 0 to raise ValueError as required. Added handling for empty data to yield nothing. Added explicit handling for size >= len(data) to yield one chunk of all data. This ensures the final partial chunk is yielded and size larger than input yields one chunk, matching the requirements and tests."}